WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.968
-Kate, you look gorgeous
and stunning as always.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:05.167
-Thanks, Jimmy!
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:09.534
Last time I saw you,
we played "That's My Jam."

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:10.901
-Oh, my God.
-And you were --

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.801
-I was nuts.
-No, you were fantastic.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.601
-Was I okay?
-You and your brother.

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:16.434
What do you mean? Okay?
All-star performance.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.067
-I feel like --
Honestly, I left there,

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.267
and I called my brother.

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:21.801
I was like, "Did I come
across, like, crazy?

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:23.734
Was I way too competitive?"

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.667
-No, you were great 'cause
you knew all the answers.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:28.234
I mean, you know music
and you can sing.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.000
And you're fun.
-I had so much fun.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.434
-You crushed it.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:33.234
-And I had never been
on a game before,

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:35.501
and I was like, "Oh,
this could be a career for me."

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.434
I just want to go
and do all these games.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.501
-It was so fun.
I was just talking about you,

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:43.100
'cause our buddy, the great
Cameron Crowe, was on the show.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.100
-He was. I saw it.
-Did you see it?

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.167
-I saw the tiny dancer when he,
like, invited you on the show.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.934
Are you going to do that?
-Yeah. I might do it.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:52.767
"Almost Famous"
is on Broadway.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:54.901
-Yes.
-So, that's the big news.

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:56.000
-Yes.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.701 --> 00:01:00.067
-I say "we" were in it.
I say "we" were in it.

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:01.868
I was barely in it.
You were in it.

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.300
-Yeah, but you were in it.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.300
-I kind of was in it,
but you're the star.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.133
And I had a little part in it.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.701
And Cameron said, "If you
want to, you can go up on stage

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:11.434
and be the manager of the..."
-Oh.

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:13.334
-And I would be like --
I know. It was amazing.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:15.400
So I met the cast.
-Were they so sweet?

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.734
-The most talented --
-I actually met the girl

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:20.434
playing Penny Lane
in Toronto,

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:22.033
when "Glass Onion"
was premiering.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:24.167
She had a movie that was
premiering, she came up to me.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.400
-No way.
And I was like --

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.901
-She's great.
-Oh, she was so sweet.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.868
-Does it bring you back?
Do you remember doing it?

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.033
Do you remember filming or no?

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:31.133
-I mean, of course.
-Right.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.567
-What do you mean?
It was so --

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:35.934
I mean, that is -- For me,
"Almost Famous" is just like --

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:39.133
I mean, it's just in my brain.
I mean, I think it'll be

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:40.901
the most memorable experience
I had.

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.734
-But Cameron told me
that people dress

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:45.267
like your character,
like Penny Lane,

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:46.934
coming to the show
in the audience.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.801
-That might feel like
a nightmare for me.

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:51.334
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.
I know. I know.

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:53.467
-Well, also just, like,
all these Penny Lanes,

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:54.934
like, what does it mean?
-Yeah.

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:56.200
-You know?
-We got to go.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.701
We have to go together.
-We have to go.

00:01:57.701 --> 00:01:59.200
Listen. I want --
If I'm going to go --

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.767
Which I definitely have to.
-Let's go together.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.801
-I can't do it alone.
I need, like, you and Billy.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:05.767
-Let's do it. Let's have
a little reunion and go.

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.734
-Oh, we had so much fun
on this movie, you guys.

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:10.501
-No, I mean, laughing and crying
laughing every single day.

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:13.167
But you crushed it. I love it.
And --

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:15.434
-I'm so happy for Cameron,
too, that, like, you know --

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.400
That must have been
really interesting for him

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.567
kind of reliving it and trying
to translate it for the stage.

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:23.501
-But, also,
it's his life, as well.

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:25.267
-Crazy.
-On top of it.

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:27.501
Did you sing on the soundtrack
of "Almost Famous" or no?

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:28.567
-No.
-You didn't sing.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:29.934
-No, no.
-Because you can sing.

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:31.634
-I love to sing.
-Yeah.

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.868
-I'm -- Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:36.167
No. I just feel weird saying
it because I --

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:39.067
-"I'm" -- You can't --
That is a cliffhanger.

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:41.501
What if you just said,
"I'm -- We'll be right back."

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:44.033
"I'm --"
-"And see you guys later."

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.334
-You're making a record?

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:47.234
-I've been making a record
for like a year.

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:48.534
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Kate!

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:51.334
-Yeah, yeah.
-Yes!

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.767
-It's so fun.
-Wait. That's fantastic.

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:56.100
-You know, I had this thing
at COVID -- everyone --

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.467
Every time you're doing
interviews, people are like,

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.267
"Do you have any regrets?"

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:02.434
I go, "I'm early 40s."
Like, not yet.

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:04.868
-"Not yet. I don't
have any regrets. Yeah.

00:03:04.868 --> 00:03:07.767
-But during COVID, I was like,
you know, what am I doing?

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:10.501
I actually write -- I've been
writing music since I was 19.

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:12.734
And, like, I've never shared it.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:15.033
And so I just thought that would
be one of my great regrets.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:17.033
Like, I have no expectations.
-Yeah. Why not just do it?

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:18.334
-I just want
to put a record out.

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:20.501
-That's exactly right.
-And so I'm doing it.

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.234
And I'm really excited.
I can't wait.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:23.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-When? Next year?

00:03:23.801 --> 00:03:26.000
-Next year. Yeah. Next year.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.501
-If you feel comfortable, come
on our show and sing a song.

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:29.667
-I will. Oh, I will.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:31.067
-We will play with you
and we'll have fun.

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:33.100
-I will definitely do that.
-Alright, buddy. I love you.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.701
Alright, I want to talk about

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.234
"Glass Onion:
A Knives Out Mystery."

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:39.133
-Yeah. Oh, my gosh.
This movie is so fun.

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:41.801
-I know. I don't want to ruin
anything or spoil anything.

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.200
I never do. So I won't.
-Okay.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.434
-But the whole cast
is great in this.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:46.534
-Well -- Yeah.

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.734
-Go.
-No, you go.

00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:51.300
-I am --

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.868
releasing an album next year.

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:55.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.634
-I -- Honestly,
this was another --

00:03:57.634 --> 00:04:00.567
I mean, you have
few great experiences.

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:03.801
Kurt always says, like,
every ten years, you know,

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:06.167
if you're lucky, you get
another great experience

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.367
making a movie, where, like,
everything kind of fits.

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.634
-Yeah. And this is one of them?
-That's what this felt like.

00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:12.601
It really was like --
-Well, it crushed.

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:14.567
It came out --
They did some experiment thing.

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:17.534
It came out in the theaters.
Crushed. I mean, broke records.

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:19.367
And then went away.
-I know.

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:21.334
-Very mysterious.
-Very.

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:23.868
-Very Glass Onion-y.
-A true "Knives Out" mystery.

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:25.934
-Yeah. What is a mystery?
What is real life?

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:29.567
-But I really feel, like, what
was so wonderful about that

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:32.133
was that we -- people
want to go to see movies.

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:34.133
-You said people
were in the crowd

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:35.968
when you went to the premiere
and it was like "Rocky."

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:37.067
-Yeah. It was like --

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:38.901
-People were screaming,
going, "Yeah!"

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:40.834
-Yeah. I mean, it was wild.

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:42.601
-That's fun.
-It was so fun.

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:44.434
-To get that experience
on a big screen.

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:45.834
-In front of 1,500 people.

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:48.634
So, the first time I saw it --
I hadn't seen it before.

00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:50.667
I saw it in front
of 1,500 people,

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:53.534
so I was already sweating
and had a bit of a migraine.

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.934
-Yeah, you're freaking out.
-Oh.

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:58.367
But the second
the crowd started,

00:04:58.367 --> 00:05:00.267
it was like --
oh, man, this is a blast.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:03.400
-It's a party. I want to read
one review that stuck out.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.701
Plug your ears
if I'm going to embarrass you.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.133
-Yeah. This is --
I don't like these things.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:10.701
-Daily Beast says, in part,
"Kate Hudson absolutely kills

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:12.334
in 'Glass Onion:
A Knives Out Mystery.'

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:14.901
Hudson steals the show.
-Oh! Ohh!

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:19.868
-It might just be her
sharpest performance yet."

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.667
-Aah!
-Come on, Kate Hudson!

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.300
Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.934
-Oh, my God!
-Ooh-la-la.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:27.601
-I love that.
That makes me feel good.

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:29.901
-That makes you feel good?
-I'm glad that you read that.

00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:31.901
